Senior direction (via fahreza): android is a tool any agent uses, not a dedicated agent. The android-pilot preset was pure prompt-convenience — its agent.yaml listed no MCP servers; tool injection was always default_mcp_servers(), independent of the preset. So deleting it costs only the canned role prompt, and that knowledge moved into mcp_android.py tool descriptions where it reaches EVERY agent: FLAG_SECURE note (black screenshot -> use screen_map) on android_screenshot, re-verify-after-acting on android_screen_map; the open_app>tap_text>tap preferences were already there. Rejected the MCP initialize 'instructions' field — couldn't verify the claude CLI surfaces it; descriptions are the guaranteed channel. Dead code noted: load_presets_from_dir/install_builtin_templates are never called, so presets come only from builtin_presets() — no stale android-pilot copies on user machines. The smartphone entry in setup's presetIcons map went with it.

HISTORY NOTE: two earlier commits today (orphaned b4bb767/3227139, reset before push) additionally gated the android MCP server behind an enabled android connector. Fahreza reverted that direction after android-handoever.md surfaced: the Linux design-review session (same day) had already ruled the connector abstraction abuse (ADR-022 contract violation, hidden global config) and decided to DELETE it + drop the cargo feature (ADR-023 always-compile precedent). 'Not enabled by default' was never a hard requirement — I over-read it; 'compiled in != works out of the box', the Android page + doctor own the runtime expectation. The handover plan (Phases A-E) executes in the commits after this one.
